falsified_when registry_c050_build4_cost_journeys_audit_modules_auth_reconciled_parity_measured == False

# C050 BUILD #5 — the `erasure` module (GDPR account-erasure), 2026-07-01. Closes the parity report's erasure-gdpr PARTIAL
# gap with a proper HYBRID module (the pattern held): npm the fail-closed ORCHESTRATOR (@suluk/better-auth's
# beforeDeleteCascade — if a cleanup step throws it ABORTS rather than half-erasing then deleting the user, so a fix flows
# via npm), OWN the wiring. erasure.service.ts: an Effect `Erasure` service (erase = run the cascade then write the
# receipt) + `sulukCascade(db)` = ordered leaf-first deleteSteps over the core Suluk tables (activity_log, cost_event,
# billing_account, key_lineage, credit_transaction — ALL key on userId, verified) via parameterized `sql`DELETE FROM
# ${sql.identifier(table)} WHERE userId = ${id}`` + `erasureHook(db)` (the Better Auth deleteUser.beforeDelete builder,
# the PROPER integration) + re-exported step/anonymizeStep constructors (the app PICKS the posture delete-vs-anonymize +
# TRIMS the cascade to installed modules). erasure.schema.ts: an OWNED erasure_receipt GDPR audit table (id/userId/posture/
# steps-JSON/erasedAt), written only AFTER the cascade succeeds (a failed/aborted erase leaves NO false "erased" record).
# erasure.routes.ts: POST /erasure/:userId (admin-gate in prod). erasure.provision.ts: 0004_erasure. registryDep app only
# (the cascade hits other modules' tables by NAME in raw SQL, no code import → decoupled; a missing table fails-closed as
# designed). @suluk/platform catalog got the erasure route entry; platform tests 10 pass (added the /erasure route +
# provision-merge assertion). Registry now 10 ITEMS. VALIDATED: 4 erasure TS transpile; `bunx shadcn build` ok all 10;
# platform 10 pass. CLEAN-ROOM PROOF (end-to-end, without touching autotoolfactory or republishing platform): a FRESH temp
# project `shadcn add MahmoodKhalil57/suluk/erasure` pulled 5 files (erasure + app via registryDep), bun install + tsc = 0
# own-code errors (the lone error is the pre-existing @suluk/openapi-compat transitive nit). FINDING: shadcn lands targets
# at ROOT (not src/) when the project has no pre-existing src/ dir — the whole tree shifts uniformly so relative imports
# still resolve. Shipped as a LIVE registry module (pushed); the @suluk/platform 0.1.2 republish + autotoolfactory adoption
# is the batch-cadence follow-up (preserves the build-#4 one-shot-from-installed-generator invariant).
claim registry_c050_build5_erasure_gdpr_cascade_module_cleanroom_proven: Bool @>=0.6 = True
falsified_when registry_c050_build5_erasure_gdpr_cascade_module_cleanroom_proven == False

# C052 — THE npm-PACKAGE vs shadcn-REGISTRY BOUNDARY RULE (2026-07-01; operator: "think what we should add as suluk
# packages and what we should keep in our shadcn registry"). Settled via a 25-agent multi-lens analysis (classify ->
# adversarial-verify -> synthesize) over the REAL inventory (~45 @suluk packages, 10 registry modules). THE RULE: a
# capability is npm-package LOGIC iff a money/security/correctness bug in it MUST flow to every consumer via npm (atomic
# CAS, cap/headroom algebra, signature/SSRF verify, status/Problem-Details mapping, deterministic contract projection); and
# since ~45 packages already exist you ALMOST NEVER spawn a new one -> you DEP the package and put only the app-owned,
# per-repo-editable WIRING (Hono routes, the Effect Context.Tag/Layer to Db/env, the drizzle schema, the provision
# fragment, app POLICY = which windows/templates/limits) in a shadcn REGISTRY module. New package ONLY for genuinely-novel
# shared logic with no existing home; EXTEND an existing package/module when the gap is a declared slot. LITMUS (both ways):
# a registry module that reimplements a package's algorithm is a fork-in-waiting; a "fully-owned" module that hides a shared
# correctness/security algorithm is the same bug. KEY FINDING: the logic layer is MATURE; growth is REGISTRY-FIRST. Of 12
# candidates classified, newPackagesNeeded = ZERO. The adversarial pass CAUGHT a wrong "new package" instinct (rate-limit
# felt like new token-bucket logic but @suluk/hono already ships enforceRateLimit + RateLimitStore + MemoryRateLimitStore;
# @suluk/cost owns the rate-limited settlement; @suluk/credits the overflow CAS) = the Adam over-build blindspot caught by
# an independent lens. VERDICTS: email/webhooks(payments)/mcp/agents/jobs(cost)/i18n/bulk-ops(drizzle)/rate-limit(hono) =
# registry-over-existing-package; keys-provision-route/uploads(deploy)/validation(hono) = extend-existing; seo =
# not-a-backend-module (build/client-time). ROADMAP (value x genericness): email -> webhooks -> keys-provision-route ->
# rate-limit -> i18n. ADR C052. This rule governs every subsequent module/package decision (each Cxxx module ADR cites it).
claim registry_c052_boundary_rule_registry_first_zero_new_packages: Bool @>=0.6 = True
falsified_when registry_c052_boundary_rule_registry_first_zero_new_packages == False

# C050 BUILD #6 — the `email` module (first roadmap item under the C052 boundary), 2026-07-01. The C052 top priority
# (blocks real signups; near-universal). Registry-over-existing-package: DEP @suluk/email (the EmailProvider transport +
