# `Email` service (send/verify/reset) + `EmailCfg` (Context.Tag) + `emailCfgFromEnv(env)` (console in dev, Resend when
# ENVIRONMENT=production AND RESEND_API_KEY AND EMAIL_FROM present) + `EmailCfgLive(env)`; EmailLive picks the provider once
# and composes verifyEmail/resetPasswordEmail templates -> provider.send. The PROPER integration is Better Auth (pass
# verify/reset into buildAuth's sendVerificationEmail + sendResetPassword); routes are the internal surface. email.routes.ts:
# POST /email/send + /email/verify. STATELESS binding — NO schema, NO provision fragment (email is a thin provider binding,
# per C052; audit via the logs module if wanted) — so the catalog entry is a route WITHOUT provision, and buildProvisionConfig
# naturally omits it. registryDep app; deps @suluk/email + effect + hono (2 files). platform tests 11 pass (added: email
# mounts /email but adds NO provision to the merge). Registry now 11 ITEMS. VALIDATED: 2 email TS transpile; `bunx shadcn
# build` ok all 11; platform 11 pass. email's real-consumer typecheck folds into the batched autotoolfactory regen (below).
claim registry_c050_build6_email_module_registry_over_suluk_email_stateless: Bool @>=0.6 = True
falsified_when registry_c050_build6_email_module_registry_over_suluk_email_stateless == False

# C050 BUILD #7 — the C052 ROADMAP batch: webhooks + rate-limit + i18n + keys-provision (2026-07-01). Four modules, ALL
# registry-over-existing-package (C052: zero new packages). webhooks/rate-limit/i18n built IN PARALLEL via a workflow (3
# builders, each grounded in the REAL package source + transpile-gated + adversarially verified: wraps-real-exports +
# no-reimplemented-logic + transpiles); keys-provision built + type-checked SOLO (coupling-heavy). (1) `webhooks` over
# @suluk/payments: POST /webhooks/stripe reads the RAW body (c.req.text(), NOT json — signature needs exact bytes),
# verifyStripeSignature (SDK-free HMAC-SHA256 stays upstream), dedups on the Stripe event id against an OWNED webhook_event
# table (onConflictDoNothing().returning() = at-least-once safe), routes via webhookRouter; documented fulfillment STUBS
# decoupled from @suluk/credits. Route + provision (0005_webhooks). Workflow CAUGHT a naming slip live: the real export is
# STRIPE_EVENTS.checkoutCompleted NOT checkoutSessionCompleted. (2) `rate-limit` over @suluk/hono: mountRateLimit(app) =
# principal-aware enforceRateLimit middleware (bucket math + RateLimitStore + 429/Retry-After stay upstream; owns only the
# keyer + store choice). (3) `i18n` over @suluk/i18n: mountI18n(app) = locale/dir negotiation middleware (?lang > cookie >
# Accept-Language; the q-weighted matcher stays upstream). BOTH stateless (no schema/provision). CORRECTION I made post-
# workflow: my prompt steered rate-limit/i18n to ROUTE mounts, but they're CROSS-CUTTING MIDDLEWARE → converted to
# middleware mounts (mountX(app) doing app.use, single-file, dropping the sub-router wrappers). (4) `keys-provision` EXTENDS
# the keys module: Keys.provision clamps a child's caps to the parent's via @suluk/keys clampChildGrant (abuse-proof), mints
# via an injected CreateKey hook (app wires Better Auth auth.api.createApiKey — minting a hashed key is auth's job),
# insertLineage; POST /keys/provision; the CreateKey requirement is per-call so existing subtree/revoke consumers are
# untouched. Registry now 14 ITEMS. VALIDATED: all files transpile; shadcn build ok all 14; keys-provision + all 4
# type-checked in autotoolfactory (real @suluk deps) = 0 own-code errors.
claim registry_c050_build7_webhooks_ratelimit_i18n_keysprovision_roadmap_batch: Bool @>=0.6 = True
falsified_when registry_c050_build7_webhooks_ratelimit_i18n_keysprovision_roadmap_batch == False
